  "id": "DrugBank_DB09143 - MONDO_6962",
  "verbalization": "Sonidegib is implicated in the pathogenesis of Sebaceous Adenocarcinoma through a chain of indications that link it to Vismodegib, which in turn is associated with this cancer. The evidence suggests that Sonidegib may act as a precursor or indirect agent in the development of Sebaceous Adenocarcinoma, as it is linked to Basal Cell Carcinoma and Sweat Gland Cancer, both of which are also associated with Vismodegib. This implies a potential role for Sonidegib in the progression of sebaceous epithelial tumors, possibly through shared molecular pathways or biological mechanisms. The high scores in the visible paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these indications highlights a possible dependency on Vismodegib, which may be a key mediator in the oncogenic process of Sebaceous Adenocarcinoma.",
